# What the image build may take from the checkout it runs in: only what the
# Dockerfile copies. The test and lint caches, the tests, and a local build or
# egg-info stay out: the build sends Docker about 2 MB of code, not the 60 MB
# a checkout that has run the tests holds. A file the Dockerfile starts to
# copy is added below, or its COPY fails.
*
!requirements.lock
!alembic.ini
!app
!migrations
!scripts

# Inside those, what a developer's machine leaves beside the code. The image
# never writes bytecode (PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE), so any it held would be a
# copy of someone's local run, and the image would differ by whose checkout
# built it. Local .env files stay out too: the image is built from the
# commit, nothing else. These come after the lines above, which they override.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.DS_Store
**/.env
**/.env.*
